  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything, because `channel` is still read downstream. Removing it from `OrderPlaced` would break another team's service.\n\n- **`analytics-ingest` requires it.** `analytics-ingest/src/core/events.ts:34` parses `channel` with `reader.oneOf(\"channel\", CHANNELS)`. Its README (lines 27 and 31) documents `channel` as part of the `OrderPlaced` contract. A missing `channel` makes ingestion reject the whole event, and `analytics-ingest/test/ingest.test.ts:88` and `:158` test exactly that. The `orders` table also has a `channel` column (`src/ingest.ts:17`, `src/core/rows.ts:8`).\n- **`billing-service` only mentions it in test fixtures.** It appears in `billing-service/test/helpers.ts:18` and `onOrderPlaced.test.ts:106`. I didn't find it used in its source, so billing is probably unaffected.\n- **Inside `orders-service`, nothing reads it after validation.** It is only validated and copied through:\n  - `core/order.ts` defines `CHANNELS`, validates the value and stores it on the order.\n  - `core/events.ts:50` copies it into the event.\n  - `api/requestParsing.ts:18` requires it on `POST /orders`.\n  - Removing it here would also drop the 400 for an invalid channel and change the documented `POST /orders` request body.\n\nYour premise that nothing reads it holds for this repo but not for the event's consumers.\n\nHow do you want to proceed?\n1. **Coordinate with the Analytics team first.** They would make `channel` optional or remove it, then we remove it here. This is the safe route.\n2. **Remove it from the order model only.** `OrderPlaced` would keep a `channel`, but we'd need to decide where its value comes from, so this is probably not what you want.\n3. **Remove it everywhere now.** This breaks `analytics-ingest`, which would reject every new `OrderPlaced` event. I'd only do this if you confirm that's acceptable.",
